0020: mesh casters for the GI server (real-time GI work package MC-2). Client export RemixBridge_GiObjects(objects, count) sends placed objects (GiObject in util/util_gi.h: object id, LITE instance, a 3x4 model-to-world matrix, a removed flag) as Bridge_GiObjects commands of at most 256 records, with no answer. The server hands each batch to the GI worker (patch 0018), which builds the index of the game's packages at the first batch (server.giMeshGame, default three levels up from .trex; server.giMeshMods, default the Documents Mods folder, "off" for none) with ts3_meshes.h, resolves each LITE to its model's caster mesh (shadow LOD, else LOD 0) and keeps the latest record of each object. Counter words 14-21 of RemixBridge_GiReadCounters: objects, models resolved, models missing, index ready, LITEs linked, index milliseconds, records dropped. The per-pixel pass (patch 0019) takes the table at its next pass: one bottom level a model, built in the pass that first needs it, and the 1024 objects nearest the camera as static instances after the capsules and boxes (custom index 0, mask 1, no culling). The [GiPixel] line and its shared words gain meshes and models. Test: test-gi-mesh.cmd (test_gi_mesh_device). The server compiles ts3_meshes.h, which native/remix-bridge/build.cmd copies in from native/remix-bridge/server.
Applies after 0019.
